-// Extended-basic-block insertion and elimination of RVV vector configuration.
-//
-// Eligible vector instructs only declare their required configuration and emit
-// their operation unconditionally. This pass inserts explicit rvv_set_config
-// nodes where needed. It tracks the (sew, vl) most recently established in each
-// block. Every setup uses m1/tu/mu with vl equal to the shape's element count.
-// Assuming vstart is zero, a matching tracked (sew, vl) means the hardware
-// already holds the required configuration and no setup node is inserted.
-// The tracked state is dropped at control-flow joins and whenever
-// an intervening node might clobber VL/VTYPE (see rvv_preserves_vsetvli), so
-// the first simple node after either always re-establishes the configuration.
-// Elimination is disabled for unsafe-marked nmethods: SIGBUS recovery may skip
-// a faulting RVV instruction without resetting vstart, violating this assumption.
@@ -1270,59 +1140,0 @@
-  if (C->max_vector_size() == 0) {
